# =============================================================================
# CCC Wiki — MASTER SECRETS & PER-ENVIRONMENT TEMPLATE
# =============================================================================
# This is the single, centralized inventory of every SECRET and every
# value that DIFFERS PER DEPLOYMENT (host, operator, environment). Non-secret
# tunables that are the same for everyone live in config.md.
#
#   - Copy to `config/.env` (gitignored) and fill in real values.
#   - `config/.env` and any `*.env` are gitignored — NEVER commit real secrets.
#   - To push these into GitHub Actions / AWS, see config.md ("How to apply").
#
# Each entry says WHERE the real value is actually consumed ("apply to:"), so
# you set it in exactly one place. This file is the map; config.md is the how-to.
#
# Classification follows the security review: an IdP signing CERT is PUBLIC
# metadata (not a credential); only private keys / passwords / API tokens are
# true secrets. Marked [SECRET] vs [PUBLIC-BUT-PER-ENV] below.
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1) LOCAL / connor-server STACK  ->  apply to: deploy/local/.env
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Docker Compose stack (BookStack + MariaDB) reads deploy/local/.env.
# `dev-up.sh` auto-generates a local-dev .env if missing; for connor-server the
# live .env is hand-maintained and is NEVER overwritten by a deploy.
# (Working template: deploy/local/.env.example — same keys, layer-local copy.)

# [SECRET] BookStack app key. Generate ONCE, then NEVER change it (rotating it
# invalidates every session + all 2FA enrolment). Generate with:
#   docker run --rm --entrypoint /bin/bash lscr.io/linuxserver/bookstack:latest appkey
APP_KEY=base64:GENERATE_ONCE_DO_NOT_REUSE_THIS_PLACEHOLDER

# [SECRET] MariaDB passwords (local container only; on AWS the DB is RDS, see §3).
DB_ROOT_PASSWORD=change-me-strong-root-password
DB_PASSWORD=change-me-strong-app-password

# [PER-ENV] The exact URL you browse to — scheme + host + port MUST match, or
# links and SAML break. LAN: http://10.76.88.214 (HTTP_BIND=80).
# SSH tunnel: http://localhost:8080 (HTTP_BIND=8080).
APP_URL=http://10.76.88.214
HTTP_BIND=80


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2) REMOTE DEPLOY TARGET  ->  apply to: shell env for deploy/local/deploy-remote.sh
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Operator-specific SSH target for `make deploy` / deploy-remote.sh. Defaults
# shown; override per machine. (Not secret, but per-operator, so it lives here.)
REMOTE_HOST=connor-server
REMOTE_DIR=ccc-wiki                 # relative to the remote $HOME


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3) AWS PRODUCTION SECRETS  ->  apply to: AWS Secrets Manager (mostly automatic)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IMPORTANT: most of these are GENERATED by `terraform apply` — you do NOT set
# them by hand. Listed here so the full secret surface is discoverable in one
# place. Paths use name_prefix (default "ccc-wiki"); see config.md.

# [AUTO] ccc-wiki/app-key          - TF-generated (random_bytes), stable in state. Do NOT rotate.
# [AUTO] ccc-wiki/breakglass-admins- TF-generated JSON {admin1,admin2}: local admin passwords for IdP outages.
# [AUTO] RDS master password       - RDS-managed (manage_master_user_password). Never in a file.

# Populate by hand during Phase 2 SSO bring-up (see config.md + the SAML runbook):
# [SECRET] ccc-wiki/saml/sp_key    - SAML SP private key (only if VUIT requires signed requests).
# [PUBLIC] ccc-wiki/saml/sp_x509   - SAML SP certificate (public cert; pairs with sp_key).
# [PUBLIC] ccc-wiki/saml/idp_x509  - VUIT IdP signing certificate (public cert; bare base64 body).
SAML_SP_KEY=PLACEHOLDER-set-during-VUIT-coordination
SAML_SP_X509=PLACEHOLDER-set-during-VUIT-coordination
SAML_IDP_X509=PLACEHOLDER-set-during-VUIT-coordination


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4) GITHUB ACTIONS SECRETS  ->  apply to: repo Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions > Secrets
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NONE are required today. CI/CD authenticates with:
#   - github.token         (auto-injected, ephemeral, per-run — not a stored secret)
#   - AWS via OIDC role    (AWS_ROLE_ARN is a repo VARIABLE, not a secret — see config.md)
# Reserved for the future features below (those credentials live in AWS Secrets
# Manager, not GitHub, because they are used by the running app, not by CI).


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5) FUTURE-FEATURE SECRETS (not yet implemented; from the open issues)
#    ->  apply to: AWS Secrets Manager when the feature lands
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [SECRET] SES SMTP credentials                 - outbound email (issue #22). Wire to BookStack MAIL_PASSWORD.
# MAIL_USERNAME=
# MAIL_PASSWORD=
# [SECRET] GitHub fine-grained PAT (issues:write only) - contact-page intake auto-files issues (#15). Least-privilege, rotated.
# CONTACT_INTAKE_GITHUB_TOKEN=
# [SECRET] BookStack API token(s)               - agent-scoped REST tokens for headless authoring (#27/#28/#29).
#                                                 Map to a low-privilege "Agent author" role; never logged.
# BOOKSTACK_API_TOKEN_ID=
# BOOKSTACK_API_TOKEN_SECRET=


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6) OPTIONAL: local SAML2 smoke test  ->  apply to: deploy/local/.env (AUTH_METHOD=saml2)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only when smoke-testing SSO wiring against a mock IdP locally. Real Vanderbilt
# Shibboleth is unreachable from the LAN. Attribute NAMES are config (see
# config.md); the IdP x509 below is a PUBLIC cert, not a secret.
# SAML2_IDP_x509=
